%U A399087 6183,6344,6375,6615,6776,6858,6859,7479,7624,7640,7749,7911,8072,8375,8775,8936,9125,9207
%N A399087 Numbers k such that k and k+1 are both biquadratefree numbers that are not cubefree (A375072).
%C A399087 First differs from A372691 at n = 14. Differs from A372691 by having the terms 2888, 6615, 6776, 6859, 8775, ..., and not having the terms 2943, 9855, 10880, 10935, 17792, ... .
%C A399087 Subsequence of A176313 and first differs from it at n = 28: A176313(28) = 5831 is not a term in this sequence.
%C A399087 Numbers k such that A051903(k) = A051903(k+1) = 3.
%C A399087 The asymptotic density of this sequence is Product_{p prime} (1 - 2/p^4) - 2 * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^3 - 1/p^4) + Product_{p prime} (1 - 2/p^3) = 0.0047576447275580778462... .
%H A399087 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399087/b399087.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A399087 emax[n_] := emax[n] = Max[FactorInteger[n][[;; , 2]]]; emax[1] = 0; Select[Range[10000], emax[#] == emax[# + 1] == 3 &]
%o A399087 (PARI) is1(k) = k > 1 && vecmax(factor(k)[, 2]) == 3;
%o A399087 isok(k) = is1(k) && is1(k+1);
%Y A399087 Intersection of A369020 and A375072.
%Y A399087 Subsequence of A046100.
%Y A399087 Cf. A004709, A051903, A176313, A372691.
